1
00:00:00,188 --> 00:00:01,188
Miss!

2
00:00:03,118 --> 00:00:04,158
Nice lady!

3
00:00:04,658 --> 00:00:05,728
Excuse me,

4
00:00:06,388 --> 00:00:08,558
I'm sorry to interrupt, but it looks like...

5
00:00:08,558 --> 00:00:10,028
the lady you were with just left.

6
00:00:14,838 --> 00:00:16,898
Mind your own business and get back to work.

7
00:00:17,768 --> 00:00:19,608
Right. Of course.

8
00:00:27,648 --> 00:00:28,778
Nice lady!

9
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:32,188
Nice lady!

10
00:00:32,788 --> 00:00:35,218
Hold on. Nice lady!

11
00:00:35,718 --> 00:00:36,718
Nice lady.

12
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:41,498
Nice lady!

13
00:00:51,308 --> 00:00:54,078
First, I think we should review the successful cases...

14
00:00:54,408 --> 00:00:57,848
of the government rehabilitation support programs.

15
00:00:58,348 --> 00:00:59,378
Also,

16
00:00:59,608 --> 00:01:02,678
Eun Seol agreed to help with this scholarship program.

17
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,948
- Ms. Ko Eun Seol? - Yes.

18
00:01:06,348 --> 00:01:07,758
Eun Seol herself...

19
00:01:08,358 --> 00:01:11,158
is a successful case of the rehabilitation program.

20
00:01:11,958 --> 00:01:14,498
When it comes to things like the necessary programs...

21
00:01:15,328 --> 00:01:16,858
or the benefits of the project,

22
00:01:16,928 --> 00:01:18,728
she'd know better than anyone else.

23
00:01:34,318 --> 00:01:36,678
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

24
00:01:40,018 --> 00:01:41,118
You should take that.

25
00:01:42,258 --> 00:01:43,258
Hello.

26
00:01:43,888 --> 00:01:47,228
Director Joo, Ms. Park got into an accident.

27
00:01:48,198 --> 00:01:49,798
What? An accident?

28
00:01:50,628 --> 00:01:52,198
Got it. I'll be right there.

29
00:01:52,398 --> 00:01:53,568
Wait, was that Hae Ra?

30
00:01:53,798 --> 00:01:55,498
An accident? What happened?

31
00:01:55,568 --> 00:01:57,568
It seems So Yeon got into an accident.

32
00:01:58,038 --> 00:02:00,138
Wasn't she out shopping with Hae Ra?

33
00:02:00,208 --> 00:02:01,408
How badly is she hurt?

34
00:02:01,608 --> 00:02:04,548
Please calm down first. I'll go check on it.

35
00:02:04,848 --> 00:02:07,548
Sure, I'll be there with Young Hoon.

36
00:02:36,138 --> 00:02:37,248
What happened?

37
00:02:41,418 --> 00:02:42,418
Kang Hae Ra.

38
00:02:43,148 --> 00:02:44,918
I asked what happened.

39
00:02:46,988 --> 00:02:49,358
I don't know. I don't know why I did that.

40
00:02:50,658 --> 00:02:51,688
I just...

41
00:02:51,828 --> 00:02:53,288
It just briefly crossed my mind.

42
00:02:54,298 --> 00:02:56,098
For a second, I wanted her...

43
00:02:56,898 --> 00:02:58,198
to disappear somewhere.

44
00:02:59,498 --> 00:03:01,398
Tell me in a way I can understand.

45
00:03:02,198 --> 00:03:04,138
Ms. Park hates my guts,

46
00:03:04,208 --> 00:03:06,538
but she's everything to Seok Jin.

47
00:03:07,978 --> 00:03:09,538
So I wanted her to disappear.

48
00:03:11,508 --> 00:03:13,448
While I was picking out clothes,

49
00:03:13,508 --> 00:03:15,418
she went outside as if she was possessed.

50
00:03:15,478 --> 00:03:17,078
I thought if I just looked the other way,

51
00:03:17,448 --> 00:03:19,218
Ms. Park would disappear somewhere.

52
00:03:19,518 --> 00:03:21,458
That's why I didn't go after her.

53
00:03:22,388 --> 00:03:24,428
But I didn't know she'd get into an accident like this.

54
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:25,788
I mean it.

55
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:28,928
Did you contact Chief Cha?

56
00:03:29,628 --> 00:03:30,698
No. Not yet.

57
00:03:32,528 --> 00:03:34,098
Contact him right away.

58
00:03:37,608 --> 00:03:38,608
Listen.

59
00:03:39,508 --> 00:03:40,778
This was just an accident.

60
00:03:41,378 --> 00:03:43,508
This didn't happen because of anything you did.

61
00:03:44,678 --> 00:03:46,148
If you act this anxious,

62
00:03:46,748 --> 00:03:48,648
Chief Cha will notice right away.

63
00:03:49,918 --> 00:03:52,088
Calm down and contact him right away.

64
00:04:01,098 --> 00:04:02,998
Once the revised sample is confirmed,

65
00:04:03,058 --> 00:04:05,428
the first mass production line has to be fully operational.

66
00:04:05,768 --> 00:04:06,998
Right, I'll check the schedule.

67
00:04:17,948 --> 00:04:18,948
Hey, Hae Ra.

68
00:04:21,318 --> 00:04:22,318
What?

69
00:04:23,478 --> 00:04:24,618
Okay, I got it.

70
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:28,288
Is something wrong?

71
00:04:29,118 --> 00:04:30,388
My mom got into an accident.

72
00:04:31,358 --> 00:04:32,658
Oh no, is she badly hurt?

73
00:04:33,088 --> 00:04:35,058
I need to go. Please wrap things up here.

74
00:04:47,068 --> 00:04:48,408
- Seok Jin, hey. - Mom.

75
00:04:49,278 --> 00:04:50,908
Mom?

76
00:04:54,018 --> 00:04:55,018
Seok Jin...

77
00:04:56,048 --> 00:04:58,588
I think she sprained her arm a little when she fell.

78
00:04:59,488 --> 00:05:00,518
What about...

79
00:05:00,858 --> 00:05:01,958
Is she hurt anywhere else?

80
00:05:02,788 --> 00:05:04,858
She wasn't hit directly by the car.

81
00:05:05,588 --> 00:05:07,958
Thankfully, it just looks like bruises.

82
00:05:08,498 --> 00:05:10,928
She seemed very shocked, so they gave her a sedative.

83
00:05:12,328 --> 00:05:14,438
Chief Cha, you must be shaken.

84
00:05:15,498 --> 00:05:18,068
But it doesn't seem like she's seriously hurt,

85
00:05:18,138 --> 00:05:19,538
so that's a relief.

86
00:05:20,568 --> 00:05:21,678
Exactly.

87
00:05:22,038 --> 00:05:25,208
You can't leave a sick person unattended for even a second.

88
00:05:41,128 --> 00:05:42,128
Chief Cha.

89
00:05:42,598 --> 00:05:43,628
Hey, honey.

90
00:05:44,898 --> 00:05:47,298
I've already spoken to the hospital director,

91
00:05:47,698 --> 00:05:49,538
so they'll move her to the VIP ward.

92
00:05:50,138 --> 00:05:51,438
A single suite is more than enough.

93
00:05:52,408 --> 00:05:53,638
Just do as you're told.

94
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:56,708
I play golf with the hospital director here.

95
00:05:57,678 --> 00:05:59,978
I've also arranged for a caregiver,

96
00:06:00,148 --> 00:06:01,218
so keep that in mind.

97
00:06:02,178 --> 00:06:03,218
Thank you.

98
00:06:03,948 --> 00:06:04,948
Well,

99
00:06:05,018 --> 00:06:06,648
you must have had quite a scare today,

100
00:06:06,718 --> 00:06:07,718
so go on in.

101
00:06:07,718 --> 00:06:09,458
So Yeon should wake up any second now.

102
00:06:10,088 --> 00:06:11,088
Right.

103
00:06:11,558 --> 00:06:12,888
- Let's go. - Okay.

104
00:06:20,798 --> 00:06:22,268
I'll stay a little longer.

105
00:06:23,098 --> 00:06:24,368
Right, sure thing.

106
00:06:41,688 --> 00:06:42,988
(Cha Seok Jin)

107
00:06:43,058 --> 00:06:44,688
Is your mother okay?

108
00:06:59,738 --> 00:07:00,738
Hey.

109
00:07:00,908 --> 00:07:01,908
Seok Jin.

110
00:07:02,178 --> 00:07:03,908
Is your mother doing okay?

111
00:07:04,848 --> 00:07:06,678
Yes, thankfully it wasn't a major accident.

112
00:07:07,178 --> 00:07:08,448
She just hurt her arm a little.

113
00:07:10,278 --> 00:07:12,218
Still, she must've been so shocked.

114
00:07:13,218 --> 00:07:14,788
Yes, I think that was the case.

115
00:07:16,918 --> 00:07:19,928
I'm sure you were really shaken up too.

116
00:07:22,128 --> 00:07:24,968
I'll make sure to visit her when I have time.

117
00:07:26,228 --> 00:07:27,468
I'd appreciate that.

118
00:07:28,238 --> 00:07:29,638
My mom will really like it too.

119
00:07:31,438 --> 00:07:32,868
Right. I'll see you at work then.

120
00:07:39,308 --> 00:07:40,308
Seok Jin.

121
00:07:41,748 --> 00:07:42,818
I'm sorry.

122
00:07:44,288 --> 00:07:45,588
This is all on me.

123
00:07:46,588 --> 00:07:49,088
It couldn't be helped. It was an accident.

124
00:07:50,888 --> 00:07:51,888
But...

125
00:07:52,628 --> 00:07:54,998
I really want to get along well with her.

126
00:07:56,128 --> 00:07:57,898
So I was trying my best.

127
00:07:59,928 --> 00:08:01,768
You're really disappointed in me, aren't you?

128
00:08:02,998 --> 00:08:03,998
No.

129
00:08:04,638 --> 00:08:06,608
This would've happened even if she was with me.

130
00:08:08,908 --> 00:08:10,708
Thanks for understanding, Seok Jin.

131
00:08:16,218 --> 00:08:17,818
I'll do better.

132
00:08:19,348 --> 00:08:20,888
To you,

133
00:08:22,288 --> 00:08:23,988
and to your mom.

134
00:08:39,068 --> 00:08:40,208
I'm home.

135
00:08:40,408 --> 00:08:41,408
Hae Ra.

136
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:43,208
Come here and sit down for a second.

137
00:08:49,178 --> 00:08:50,178
Oh, boy.

138
00:08:52,488 --> 00:08:53,518
Hae Ra,

139
00:08:54,518 --> 00:08:56,688
are you sure you can handle being with Chief Cha?

140
00:08:57,188 --> 00:08:58,388
What do you mean by that?

141
00:08:58,488 --> 00:09:00,658
This incident must've made you realise...

142
00:09:01,228 --> 00:09:04,028
what kind of guy the man you chose actually is.

143
00:09:05,368 --> 00:09:06,698
He's already so rigid,

144
00:09:06,768 --> 00:09:08,268
and he has a sick parent on top of that.

145
00:09:09,098 --> 00:09:10,498
Are you prepared for that?

146
00:09:10,798 --> 00:09:12,368
Why would you ask me that, Dad?

147
00:09:12,838 --> 00:09:14,738
Did you date Mom fully prepared from the start?

148
00:09:16,208 --> 00:09:17,338
Kang Hae Ra.

149
00:09:17,438 --> 00:09:19,008
You know I'm right.

150
00:09:19,678 --> 00:09:22,218
Mom's family couldn't even compare to yours.

151
00:09:22,418 --> 00:09:24,048
Were you able to handle them from the beginning?

152
00:09:24,218 --> 00:09:26,718
You just endured it because you loved her.

153
00:09:28,988 --> 00:09:30,158
I will endure it all, too.

154
00:09:40,938 --> 00:09:41,938
Hey.

155
00:09:43,098 --> 00:09:44,098
Honey.

156
00:09:44,938 --> 00:09:46,538
Please understand her.

157
00:09:47,308 --> 00:09:49,338
Hae Ra likes Chief Cha a lot.

158
00:09:49,708 --> 00:09:52,948
What can we do when our daughter's crazy about him?

159
00:09:52,948 --> 00:09:55,448
All we can do is support them.

160
00:09:56,648 --> 00:09:57,718
Chief Cha...

161
00:09:58,288 --> 00:09:59,848
I'm just not entirely happy with him.

162
00:10:00,988 --> 00:10:03,418
He's too rigid and lacks flexibility completely.

163
00:10:03,788 --> 00:10:05,058
Maybe it's due to his background,

164
00:10:05,628 --> 00:10:07,188
but he's driven in a negative way.

165
00:10:07,998 --> 00:10:09,898
I actually like Chief Cha.

166
00:10:12,228 --> 00:10:14,938
He kept his principles despite his difficult background.

167
00:10:15,168 --> 00:10:17,838
And above all, he takes care of his sick parent.

168
00:10:18,608 --> 00:10:20,368
Seeing him bear all the responsibility...

169
00:10:20,608 --> 00:10:22,238
makes me feel proud, yet sorry for him.

170
00:10:22,808 --> 00:10:26,378
I also like that he's upright and uncompromising.

171
00:10:27,408 --> 00:10:28,948
You're unbelievable.

172
00:10:29,278 --> 00:10:31,118
We always have completely opposite points of view.

173
00:10:32,518 --> 00:10:34,558
That's why we were drawn to each other.

174
00:10:35,588 --> 00:10:36,758
But you know what?

175
00:10:37,628 --> 00:10:40,158
Looking closely at Chief Cha,

176
00:10:40,488 --> 00:10:42,758
he strangely resembles you.

177
00:10:44,628 --> 00:10:45,628
Me?

178
00:10:45,668 --> 00:10:48,698
Yes. You've softened up over time,

179
00:10:49,068 --> 00:10:51,108
but in your younger days, you were every bit as rigid...

180
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:52,308
and uncompromising.

181
00:10:52,538 --> 00:10:55,308
No one was a bigger perfectionist at work.

182
00:10:56,038 --> 00:10:57,648
Sometimes when I look at Chief Cha,

183
00:10:57,978 --> 00:11:00,208
I feel like I'm looking at a younger version of you.

184
00:11:02,048 --> 00:11:03,778
Is that so?

185
00:11:11,888 --> 00:11:14,598
So, did anything happen with Chief Cha?

186
00:11:15,458 --> 00:11:16,858
He understood.

187
00:11:18,368 --> 00:11:19,528
Did you play your part?

188
00:11:19,928 --> 00:11:21,968
Yes, thankfully it went smoothly.

189
00:11:22,398 --> 00:11:24,668
It's unfortunate that So Yeon got hurt,

190
00:11:24,738 --> 00:11:25,808
but this incident...

191
00:11:25,808 --> 00:11:28,538
must've made Chief Cha clearly realise his place.

192
00:11:29,508 --> 00:11:30,738
What do you mean by that?

193
00:11:31,378 --> 00:11:35,248
Even the CEO stepped up today to take care of So Yeon.

194
00:11:35,748 --> 00:11:37,278
You think so?

195
00:11:39,588 --> 00:11:43,818
We need something more concrete to lock in Chief Cha's feelings.

196
00:11:44,358 --> 00:11:45,388
What would that be?

197
00:11:48,398 --> 00:11:51,468
By the way, you two promised to get married,

198
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:53,198
but you don't even have matching rings?

199
00:11:54,698 --> 00:11:56,168
I want to get them,

200
00:11:56,838 --> 00:11:58,008
but he isn't into the idea.

201
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:00,838
He hates making people feel burdened or something.

202
00:12:02,938 --> 00:12:05,578
It'd be good to make a clear statement this time.

203
00:12:06,178 --> 00:12:09,078
If you make your relationship with Chief Cha public...

204
00:12:09,078 --> 00:12:10,248
using couple rings,

205
00:12:10,518 --> 00:12:12,648
the CEO will accept him as his future son-in-law.

206
00:12:30,938 --> 00:12:33,708
Joo Ae Sook, have you been well?

207
00:12:34,538 --> 00:12:38,248
It's me. Your husband, An Guk Cheol.

208
00:12:47,488 --> 00:12:49,888
Boss, I need to use the restroom.

209
00:12:50,958 --> 00:12:53,058
How many times has it been today?

210
00:12:53,258 --> 00:12:54,798
Gosh, don't ask.

211
00:12:55,158 --> 00:12:56,528
Did something I ate yesterday go bad?

212
00:13:10,308 --> 00:13:12,808
Wait, do you think you have food poisoning?

213
00:13:13,978 --> 00:13:15,018
I doubt it.

214
00:13:16,078 --> 00:13:18,588
I mean, how can you eat perfectly good food...

215
00:13:18,888 --> 00:13:20,388
and get an upset stomach?

216
00:13:21,788 --> 00:13:23,118
Peculiar, right?

217
00:13:23,318 --> 00:13:24,588
What did you eat?

218
00:13:24,928 --> 00:13:26,988
My dad cooked yesterday for the first time in ages,

219
00:13:27,758 --> 00:13:29,428
and this happens sometimes when I eat his food.

220
00:13:30,028 --> 00:13:32,898
Who usually cooks? Your grandmother?

221
00:13:32,898 --> 00:13:34,468
That would be a disaster.

222
00:13:35,038 --> 00:13:38,838
My grandmother is widely known to be a terrible cook.

223
00:13:39,138 --> 00:13:41,508
Don't tell me you make Eun Seol do it.

224
00:13:43,078 --> 00:13:46,508
We have a conscience, you know. How could we make her cook?

225
00:13:47,208 --> 00:13:48,678
She's the sole breadwinner for the family right now.

226
00:13:55,318 --> 00:13:58,258
We always ate well when my mom was still alive.

227
00:14:00,188 --> 00:14:01,758
Her cooking was amazing.

228
00:14:04,058 --> 00:14:06,468
But ever since she passed away,

229
00:14:06,798 --> 00:14:08,368
we just make do with whatever we have.

230
00:14:12,208 --> 00:14:14,678
If my grandmother's spending the day with her friends,

231
00:14:15,538 --> 00:14:16,778
what am I going to eat?

232
00:14:19,778 --> 00:14:22,418
Then come over to my place after closing.

233
00:14:24,588 --> 00:14:25,618
What?

234
00:14:26,388 --> 00:14:27,648
Wait, really?

235
00:14:28,118 --> 00:14:31,858
A rehabilitation program for prison inmates?

236
00:14:32,058 --> 00:14:35,658
Yes. Instead of a program that just hands out scholarships,

237
00:14:35,998 --> 00:14:38,298
I'm planning a true social giveback program...

238
00:14:38,298 --> 00:14:41,168
that gives young people a second chance.

239
00:14:42,038 --> 00:14:44,668
Honey, the scholarship foundation program...

240
00:14:44,968 --> 00:14:46,638
is first and foremost...

241
00:14:47,138 --> 00:14:49,678
about improving our corporate image.

242
00:14:50,078 --> 00:14:51,978
To build public trust,

243
00:14:52,478 --> 00:14:55,178
we don't need to take on a risk like this.

244
00:14:55,618 --> 00:14:58,388
Why bother supporting such individuals...

245
00:15:06,628 --> 00:15:08,728
- Hey, Seok Jin. - Come on in.

246
00:15:08,728 --> 00:15:10,528
- Have a seat. - Goodness.

247
00:15:12,498 --> 00:15:14,698
How's your mother doing?

248
00:15:15,098 --> 00:15:19,108
She'll be discharged in three days, but she'll only require light rehab.

249
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,878
Well, it's a huge relief it wasn't any worse.

250
00:15:22,078 --> 00:15:23,738
Thanks to Hae Ra being there,

251
00:15:23,808 --> 00:15:25,778
she was able to get to the hospital quickly.

252
00:15:26,078 --> 00:15:27,108
Right.

253
00:15:30,618 --> 00:15:31,618
And this.

254
00:15:33,018 --> 00:15:35,788
I appreciate all that you did for us.

255
00:15:36,358 --> 00:15:38,588
Thank you for getting my mother a hospital room.

256
00:15:39,028 --> 00:15:40,588
I prepared a small gift for the holidays.

257
00:15:40,588 --> 00:15:43,458
- Oh, my. - What is this?

258
00:15:43,698 --> 00:15:46,698
They say it's good for managing blood sugar after meals.

259
00:15:46,828 --> 00:15:48,738
Goodness, thank you.

260
00:15:49,398 --> 00:15:52,868
My husband needs to start watching his blood sugar now, too.

261
00:15:53,038 --> 00:15:56,338
Why don't we try it? You should have one, too.

262
00:15:56,408 --> 00:15:58,448
- I'll have one. - Let's try one each.

263
00:15:59,108 --> 00:16:00,178
Here.

264
00:16:00,878 --> 00:16:02,848
- Is it one pill per serving? - Yes, that's correct.

265
00:16:03,618 --> 00:16:04,618
I see.

266
00:16:06,718 --> 00:16:09,058
This is nice. It's easy to take.

267
00:16:09,058 --> 00:16:10,788
The moment I had it,

268
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:13,858
I could smell a hint of pine.

269
00:16:13,858 --> 00:16:15,398
It was really fragrant.

270
00:16:16,528 --> 00:16:19,998
Chief Cha, you're always so thoughtful.

271
00:16:20,668 --> 00:16:22,998
Please don't forget to take them after your meals.

272
00:16:23,138 --> 00:16:24,198
- Chief Cha. - Yes?

273
00:16:24,268 --> 00:16:25,268
While your mother's in the hospital,

274
00:16:25,338 --> 00:16:27,368
please let me know if you need anything at all.

275
00:16:27,538 --> 00:16:29,508
I'll speak to the hospital director.

276
00:16:29,778 --> 00:16:31,008
Right, thank you.

277
00:16:31,108 --> 00:16:32,478
(Ildong Investigation Services)

278
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:35,618
An Guk Cheol?

279
00:16:36,718 --> 00:16:38,148
You have to find him as soon as possible.

280
00:16:38,248 --> 00:16:39,388
You know...

281
00:16:40,488 --> 00:16:43,558
I mean, just look at this.

282
00:16:43,618 --> 00:16:47,488
With only this basic personal info to go on,

283
00:16:47,488 --> 00:16:50,598
it's bound to take both time and money.

284
00:16:51,428 --> 00:16:53,198
I don't care what it costs.

285
00:16:53,468 --> 00:16:56,138
Just find out every detail about his past.

286
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:57,798
Oh, my.

287
00:16:58,408 --> 00:17:00,808
Seeing you this worked up,

288
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:02,308
makes me think...

289
00:17:02,508 --> 00:17:05,508
Is he an ex-boyfriend who ran off with your money?

290
00:17:06,878 --> 00:17:09,918
Watch your mouth and just do what you're told!

291
00:17:11,648 --> 00:17:12,648
Right, of course.

292
00:17:13,318 --> 00:17:14,718
I'll get right on it.

293
00:17:31,468 --> 00:17:33,138
As always, you're the last one to leave.

294
00:17:34,038 --> 00:17:35,378
Did everyone go to lunch?

295
00:17:35,908 --> 00:17:36,908
Yes.

296
00:17:38,008 --> 00:17:39,548
Let's grab lunch, too.

297
00:17:40,248 --> 00:17:41,308
What should we get?

298
00:17:41,718 --> 00:17:45,688
I'm sorry, but I have plans during lunch today.

299
00:17:46,018 --> 00:17:47,318
Oh, really?

300
00:17:48,088 --> 00:17:50,818
What can you do? Either way, there's always tomorrow.

301
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:54,758
It must be something important.

302
00:17:55,398 --> 00:17:57,898
Yes, there's someone I need to see.

303
00:18:04,598 --> 00:18:06,868
What? Nice lady, hi.

304
00:18:07,808 --> 00:18:09,238
Are you feeling okay?

305
00:18:09,908 --> 00:18:11,078
I'm okay.

306
00:18:11,508 --> 00:18:12,708
Yesterday,

307
00:18:12,848 --> 00:18:15,518
I banged right into a car.

308
00:18:15,778 --> 00:18:18,388
My arm hurts a bit, but I'm fine.

309
00:18:20,488 --> 00:18:21,988
That must have hurt a lot.

310
00:18:23,458 --> 00:18:24,618
I'm okay.

311
00:18:25,128 --> 00:18:26,158
You know,

312
00:18:26,828 --> 00:18:29,428
I actually saw you that day.

313
00:18:30,498 --> 00:18:31,528
What?

314
00:18:31,898 --> 00:18:35,568
I thought it was you, so I ran after you.

315
00:18:35,638 --> 00:18:37,838
That's how I got hit by the car.

316
00:18:40,038 --> 00:18:41,108
Really?

317
00:18:41,878 --> 00:18:45,308
Yes. But it's okay. Everything's fine.

318
00:18:45,978 --> 00:18:48,218
By the way, nice lady,

319
00:18:48,718 --> 00:18:50,218
do you want some orange juice?

320
00:18:50,978 --> 00:18:52,888
No, I'm good.

321
00:18:56,318 --> 00:18:58,588
Anyway, what's that?

322
00:18:59,088 --> 00:19:00,088
Oh, this?

323
00:19:00,228 --> 00:19:02,998
I thought you might be bored alone.

324
00:19:03,858 --> 00:19:06,568
So I brought this. Do you like it?

325
00:19:07,898 --> 00:19:11,098
Gosh, I love colouring books.

326
00:19:11,868 --> 00:19:14,468
No way. It's so pretty.

327
00:19:17,908 --> 00:19:20,248
I'm going to colour the dress pink.

328
00:19:20,248 --> 00:19:21,308
Sounds good.

329
00:19:21,848 --> 00:19:23,778
- Isn't it pretty? - It is.

330
00:19:24,748 --> 00:19:26,588
What are you colouring that in with?

331
00:19:26,588 --> 00:19:28,218
This one? Green.

332
00:19:28,518 --> 00:19:30,718
- How about sky blue? - Sky blue? I like it.

333
00:19:32,628 --> 00:19:34,558
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

334
00:19:37,858 --> 00:19:38,898
Are you busy?

335
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,538
Yes, the opening event is coming up real soon.

336
00:19:43,698 --> 00:19:45,808
Even if you're busy, can you look at me for a second?

337
00:19:48,208 --> 00:19:49,208
Sure.

338
00:19:50,438 --> 00:19:51,438
Ta-da.

339
00:19:51,908 --> 00:19:52,948
What's that?

340
00:19:53,008 --> 00:19:54,918
What else? It's one of our couple rings.

341
00:19:57,418 --> 00:20:00,188
Usually, the guy is supposed to do this.

342
00:20:00,488 --> 00:20:01,558
You know that, right?

343
00:20:03,658 --> 00:20:05,288
Thank goodness it fits perfectly.

344
00:20:07,488 --> 00:20:08,958
I told you I didn't need a ring.

345
00:20:10,328 --> 00:20:14,168
I'm not just telling you to wear it. There's a reason for it.

346
00:20:15,468 --> 00:20:16,538
What reason?

347
00:20:17,268 --> 00:20:19,308
This will just make the employees uncomfortable.

348
00:20:19,368 --> 00:20:21,268
They already know what kind of relationship we have,

349
00:20:21,538 --> 00:20:22,938
so is there a need to go this far?

350
00:20:23,108 --> 00:20:24,608
Just wear it, will you?

351
00:20:26,748 --> 00:20:28,418
It's all because of my dad.

352
00:20:29,918 --> 00:20:33,048
We have to do at least this much so he knows how serious we are.

353
00:20:34,118 --> 00:20:35,888
He needs to know so he'll accept us.

354
00:20:38,118 --> 00:20:40,488
Don't you want my dad's approval?

355
00:20:43,758 --> 00:20:46,428
So don't take it off and always wear it.

356
00:20:47,168 --> 00:20:48,198
Got it?

357
00:20:55,508 --> 00:20:56,708
Mom, it's me.

358
00:20:56,978 --> 00:20:58,778
Hey, Mr. Seok Jin.

359
00:21:02,348 --> 00:21:03,348
What are you up to?

360
00:21:04,278 --> 00:21:07,148
I'm going to colour all of this today.

361
00:21:07,648 --> 00:21:08,658
Isn't it pretty?

362
00:21:09,088 --> 00:21:10,088
What is this?

363
00:21:10,658 --> 00:21:12,528
Don't you know what a colouring book is?

364
00:21:13,728 --> 00:21:15,098
Where did you get it?

365
00:21:15,528 --> 00:21:17,198
The nice lady gave it to me.

366
00:21:18,668 --> 00:21:19,728
The nice lady?

367
00:21:20,098 --> 00:21:21,098
Yes.

368
00:21:21,268 --> 00:21:23,838
The nice lady thought I might be bored,

369
00:21:23,838 --> 00:21:25,238
so she gave it to me as a gift.

370
00:21:26,568 --> 00:21:28,008
When did the nice lady come by?

371
00:21:29,608 --> 00:21:32,178
She came by earlier today.

372
00:21:42,458 --> 00:21:45,058
No way, how is this possible?

373
00:21:45,488 --> 00:21:47,158
How can everything be so delicious?

374
00:21:47,228 --> 00:21:51,298
It's delicious, right? My mom is seriously the best cook.

375
00:21:51,828 --> 00:21:54,168
She's seriously the absolute best.

376
00:21:56,138 --> 00:21:58,268
Teun Teun, hurry up and dig in.

377
00:21:58,708 --> 00:22:00,708
I didn't want to eat today,

378
00:22:00,838 --> 00:22:03,408
but seeing you eat made me super hungry.

379
00:22:03,838 --> 00:22:06,108
- I want some too. - Right, go ahead.

380
00:22:08,048 --> 00:22:09,048
What...

381
00:22:11,988 --> 00:22:14,918
Boss, you really have magic hands for cooking.

382
00:22:15,988 --> 00:22:18,188
Seriously. You have a magic touch.

383
00:22:18,558 --> 00:22:20,028
It's so precious.

384
00:22:20,558 --> 00:22:21,558
What the...

385
00:22:24,658 --> 00:22:26,868
Boss, if it's okay with you,

386
00:22:27,398 --> 00:22:29,068
could I please have one more bowl of rice?

387
00:22:45,388 --> 00:22:46,818
Why is he making a fuss holding my hand?

388
00:22:59,828 --> 00:23:02,638
You're helping the Chairman with the new scholarship program?

389
00:23:03,398 --> 00:23:07,038
Yes, I plan to help out as much as I can.

390
00:23:07,608 --> 00:23:10,138
I know you mean well,

391
00:23:11,308 --> 00:23:13,578
but I'm a little concerned.

392
00:23:16,248 --> 00:23:17,918
Given the nature of the scholarship program,

393
00:23:18,348 --> 00:23:21,448
people are bound to dig into your past.

394
00:23:21,888 --> 00:23:25,288
Is there a need to voluntarily wear the Scarlet Letter?

395
00:23:28,398 --> 00:23:31,928
I don't look at my past as a Scarlet Letter.

396
00:23:33,098 --> 00:23:34,998
Besides, hiding my past isn't going to erase it.

397
00:23:35,568 --> 00:23:39,368
It's unfair that I spent ten years in prison after being framed,

398
00:23:40,838 --> 00:23:42,438
but that's all the more reason I need to show them...

399
00:23:43,838 --> 00:23:45,248
I didn't break...

400
00:23:46,448 --> 00:23:47,908
after enduring something like that.

401
00:23:51,278 --> 00:23:52,648
And for someone out there,

402
00:23:52,718 --> 00:23:54,918
I think my story could become a source of hope.

403
00:23:57,088 --> 00:24:00,088
Eun Seol, you're much stronger than I thought.

404
00:24:00,988 --> 00:24:02,628
I worried for nothing.

405
00:24:03,228 --> 00:24:04,228
Gosh, no.

406
00:24:04,358 --> 00:24:07,328
I didn't know you'd care for me this much, Ms. Joo.

407
00:24:07,998 --> 00:24:10,338
Of course I care. You're my friend's daughter.

408
00:24:10,598 --> 00:24:13,568
If only for Hee Jung's sake, I should care at least this much.

409
00:24:14,868 --> 00:24:16,338
Thank you, Ms. Joo.

410
00:24:17,678 --> 00:24:20,678
If you need help in the future, feel free to contact me anytime.

411
00:24:21,548 --> 00:24:25,848
And keep me posted on the progress of the scholarship program.

412
00:24:26,048 --> 00:24:28,218
I'm sure there will be things I can help with from the side.

413
00:24:28,858 --> 00:24:29,858
Sure.

414
00:24:47,568 --> 00:24:49,808
I wanted to get something a bit more flashy,

415
00:24:50,908 --> 00:24:53,548
but Seok Jin doesn't really enjoy the attention.

416
00:24:55,478 --> 00:24:58,118
Still, I'm planning on getting a luxury wedding ring,

417
00:24:58,418 --> 00:25:01,688
something as flashy and noticeable as possible.

418
00:25:02,158 --> 00:25:03,618
No matter how fancy the ring is,

419
00:25:03,618 --> 00:25:05,688
if the person wearing it lacks sincerity,

420
00:25:05,758 --> 00:25:06,928
what's the point?

421
00:25:07,758 --> 00:25:09,158
It'll get in the way for no reason.

422
00:25:09,328 --> 00:25:11,528
What? It'll get in the way?

423
00:25:12,428 --> 00:25:15,638
Hey, do you even have a ring like this to be saying that?

424
00:25:17,138 --> 00:25:21,008
If your feelings are real, is there any reason to show it off?

425
00:25:24,538 --> 00:25:25,548
Whatever.

426
00:25:32,918 --> 00:25:33,918
Right.

427
00:25:38,988 --> 00:25:41,758
See, it has to be at least this good.

428
00:25:41,828 --> 00:25:43,228
I can do this much, too.

429
00:25:43,498 --> 00:25:45,668
Everyone learns off the internet these days.

430
00:25:45,928 --> 00:25:47,828
All you have to do is follow the recipe.

431
00:25:48,868 --> 00:25:53,108
Mom, that only works for people who actually have a feel for it.

432
00:25:53,438 --> 00:25:55,938
You need to know how to season food properly.

433
00:25:55,938 --> 00:26:00,878
People like us have to get out there and at least put in the legwork.

434
00:26:01,948 --> 00:26:04,048
Fortune favours those who help themselves, remember?

435
00:26:04,548 --> 00:26:06,248
Knock, and the door will be opened.

436
00:26:06,448 --> 00:26:08,188
What if knocking doesn't work?

437
00:26:08,558 --> 00:26:09,618
Then you keep knocking.

438
00:26:09,688 --> 00:26:11,758
Eventually, they'll open the door just to shut you up.

439
00:26:11,758 --> 00:26:12,858
Put in the effort.

440
00:26:13,628 --> 00:26:16,898
You talk too much. Effort, my foot.

441
00:26:17,498 --> 00:26:20,498
Do you think you'll hit the jackpot if you try hard enough?

442
00:26:20,498 --> 00:26:22,268
Who said anything about a jackpot?

443
00:26:22,438 --> 00:26:24,698
The core value of the Cheongma Scholarship Foundation...

444
00:26:24,868 --> 00:26:27,108
goes beyond simple financial support.

445
00:26:27,108 --> 00:26:29,108
It's about helping youth with potential...

446
00:26:29,178 --> 00:26:31,608
grow into the leaders of our society...

447
00:26:31,678 --> 00:26:34,508
by laying the groundwork to nurture future talents.

448
00:26:34,578 --> 00:26:36,018
Joo Mi Ran?

449
00:26:36,548 --> 00:26:39,588
I only know that she's doing well at some large company.

450
00:26:40,348 --> 00:26:41,988
Oh, really?

451
00:26:43,358 --> 00:26:45,358
I heard she changed her name.

452
00:26:46,358 --> 00:26:47,488
To Joo Mi Ran, I believe.

453
00:26:49,598 --> 00:26:53,198
Oh, my gosh. I hit the jackpot!

454
00:26:53,928 --> 00:26:55,438
What? The jackpot?

455
00:26:57,938 --> 00:27:01,168
What? No, it's nothing.

456
00:27:03,378 --> 00:27:06,908
Why did you suddenly jump up while eating?

457
00:27:06,978 --> 00:27:08,208
You startled me.

458
00:27:11,918 --> 00:27:14,718
(Cheongma)

459
00:27:17,188 --> 00:27:18,858
Getting couple rings...

460
00:27:20,158 --> 00:27:22,358
means they're officially announcing...

461
00:27:22,658 --> 00:27:24,598
their relationship, right?

462
00:27:28,168 --> 00:27:29,198
That's right.

463
00:27:29,738 --> 00:27:31,498
People get them when they want to show off...

464
00:27:31,498 --> 00:27:33,108
that they're officially together.

465
00:27:36,638 --> 00:27:39,048
Why? Did someone get matching rings?

466
00:27:40,778 --> 00:27:41,808
What?

467
00:27:42,178 --> 00:27:43,978
Who got them?

468
00:27:44,718 --> 00:27:46,748
You know, people from work.

469
00:27:48,958 --> 00:27:50,788
They must've wanted to end their secret relationship.

470
00:27:56,158 --> 00:28:00,298
Cheongma's survival this season depends on the launch of Shoejoy.

471
00:28:01,568 --> 00:28:03,368
If we don't meet the expectations of the buyers...

472
00:28:03,368 --> 00:28:05,808
and the board of directors during the evaluation,

473
00:28:06,208 --> 00:28:07,868
we won't have a future.

474
00:28:09,838 --> 00:28:12,078
There's no room for error here.

475
00:28:12,708 --> 00:28:14,248
With these evaluation results,

476
00:28:15,878 --> 00:28:18,018
I'm going to prove that your trust in me...

477
00:28:18,688 --> 00:28:19,988
was justified, sir.

478
00:28:22,558 --> 00:28:24,158
Did everyone hear that?

479
00:28:25,888 --> 00:28:28,928
Since Chief Cha is that confident,

480
00:28:28,928 --> 00:28:32,828
the rest of the executives here had better watch closely.

481
00:28:33,628 --> 00:28:35,598
Let's see whether his words are pure bluff,

482
00:28:36,438 --> 00:28:39,268
or if he actually has what it takes to lead Cheongma into the future.

483
00:28:49,148 --> 00:28:51,148
I made a reservation at a great restaurant for lunch.

484
00:28:51,618 --> 00:28:52,648
Sounds good.

485
00:28:52,718 --> 00:28:54,118
- Hello. - Hello.

486
00:30:04,058 --> 00:30:07,758
(A Trap Called Desire)

487
00:30:08,028 --> 00:30:11,758
Write down all the businesses or shops you want to run.

488
00:30:11,828 --> 00:30:14,368
Who knows? We might win the lottery someday.

489
00:30:14,928 --> 00:30:17,898
Why don't we start preparing for our wedding?

490
00:30:17,898 --> 00:30:19,368
If you're going to marry me,

491
00:30:19,438 --> 00:30:21,138
you need to get used to those kinds of gatherings.

492
00:30:21,238 --> 00:30:23,378
People who are born with a servile mindset...

493
00:30:23,438 --> 00:30:25,078
are just beyond saving.

494
00:30:25,078 --> 00:30:27,108
Ko Eun Seol always bothered me.

495
00:30:27,178 --> 00:30:30,248
You can't ignore the environment someone was born and raised in.

496
00:30:30,318 --> 00:30:31,548
Things are urgent,

497
00:30:31,618 --> 00:30:33,418
so we need to move up the interview dates.

498
00:30:33,488 --> 00:30:34,748
Just you wait, Joo Ae Sook.

499
00:30:34,818 --> 00:30:36,918
I'll soon bring you your biological daughter.

500
00:30:36,988 --> 00:30:38,618
For our Eun Seol,

501
00:30:38,828 --> 00:30:41,728
I need to step up and be a proper grandmother.
